-- title:
--   Rotation-invariant holomorphic functions on a disc factor through z^e
-- statement:
--   Let $e$ be a natural number with $0 < e$, let $\omega \in \mathbb{C}$ be a primitive $e$-th root of unity in the sense of Mathlib's `IsPrimitiveRoot`, let $r$ be a real number with $0 < r$, and let $f : \mathbb{C} \to \mathbb{C}$ be a function that is analytic on a neighbourhood of each point of the open ball $B(0,r) \subseteq \mathbb{C}$ (that is, `AnalyticOnNhd ℂ f (Metric.ball 0 r)`: for every $z$ with $|z| < r$, $f$ is analytic at $z$). Assume $f$ is invariant under the rotation by $\omega$ on that ball: $f(\omega z) = f(z)$ for all $z$ with $|z| < r$. The conclusion asserts the existence of a function $F : \mathbb{C} \to \mathbb{C}$ which is analytic at every point of the ball $B(0, r^{e})$ and satisfies $f(z) = F(z^{e})$ for all $z$ with $|z| < r$. Note that $F$ is asserted to be a function on all of $\mathbb{C}$, analytic only on $B(0,r^e)$, and the factorisation identity is claimed only on $B(0,r)$.
--
--   This is the standard local statement underlying the construction of a local parameter at an elliptic point of a modular curve: a holomorphic function on a disc invariant under the cyclic group generated by $z \mapsto \omega z$ is a holomorphic function of $z^{e}$. It is used in the analysis of sections on the modular curve, via [`ModularCurve.JZero.exists_hyperplaneSection_sum_log_secVal_ge`](thm.html#ModularCurve.JZero.exists_hyperplaneSection_sum_log_secVal_ge).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_Complex_exists_analyticOnNhd_comp_pow_of_forall_mul_eq.lean

